    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/awards-and-recognition/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Awards and Recognition - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Awards and Recognition In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here Inspiring Leadership and Outstanding Contributions The University of Saint Francis regularly recognizes the hard work, commitment, and impact of its faculty and staff. Honoring Our Mission Each year, Saint Francis employees are able to nominate an employee (staff or faculty member) for the Franciscan Spirit Award, which celebrates a faculty or staff member who exemplifies the Core Values . Celebrating Milestones Saint Francis employees are recognized for their duration of service and other milestones at our annual Employee Recognition Event. Recognizing Excellence Each year, students nominate faculty members for the Leepoxy Award. This award honors those who strive to make a difference in the lives of others through their commitment to the student learning process and the vision of higher education. Our Teaching Excellence and Campus Leadership Award annually honors an exceptional faculty member for excellence in the classroom and leadership within the Saint Francis or Fort Wayne community. Each year, the Saint Francis’ Staff Excellence Award recognizes a member of the staff for their innovative leadership of the campus community and their commitment to the process of improvement. Contact Us Human Resources St. Michael Hall Offices 203-205 Email: hr@sf.edu Hours Monday – Friday: 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    },
    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/benefits/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Benefits - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Benefits In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here Employee Benefits Overview The University of Saint Francis is committed to the health and well-being of its employees. The following benefits are available to benefit-eligible employees. Health/Healthcare Solution Employees and their dependents are eligible to participate in the Remodel Health/Healthcare Solution.  Employees will partner with Remodel Health to determine a healthcare solution. Dental and Vision Plan A Dental/Vision plan is available for employees and eligible dependents. Health Savings Accounts and Flexible Spending Accounts Health Savings Accounts (HSAs) and Flexible Spending Accounts (FSAs) are available for appropriate healthcare and dependent care expenses. Life Insurance Saint Francis provides its full-time and part-time employees with basic life insurance (AD & D: Accidental Death & Dismemberment insurance). Retirement Plan Saint Francis offers a generous 403(b) retirement account. Benefit-eligible employees can open the account upon hire and begin making pre-tax contributions. After a full year of employment, the university will match contributions up to 6% and give a 2% gift, with a 3-year vesting schedule. Vacation/Sick Time Vacation and sick time is available to all eligible employees. Paid Holidays In keeping with our Catholic values, the university is closed on the following holidays: Good Friday Easter Monday Memorial Day Independence Day Labor Day Thanksgiving and the following day Christmas Break, including Christmas Day and New Year’s Day Mission Leave The Saint Francis Mission Leave Policy encourages and supports employees to more fully embrace and embody the University of Saint Francis mission and core values through leading lives of virtue, service and joy.. This policy allows employees to voluntarily participate, with pay, in university events and community service activities that occur during regularly scheduled work hours. Tuition Benefit Program 100% employee discount after 90 days of employment (undergraduate and graduate programs) 100% discount for qualified family members of full-time employees after one year of employment (undergrad only) Discounts may be used at Saint Francis or other programs within the tuition exchange programs Employee responsible for books, fees, and room & board Contact Us Human Resources St. Michael Hall Offices 203-205 Email: hr@sf.edu Hours Monday – Friday: 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    },
    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/current-openings/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Current Openings - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Current Openings In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here Employment Application Process After completing an application for one of the openings listed below, you will receive a message on the website that your application was submitted. The search timeline for each open position varies due to the specific nature of the jobs. We are committed to keeping all applicants informed about their status during the hiring process to the best of our ability, you can expect communications regarding your application status via email as decisions are made. You may be asked to submit a statement in which you articulate your understanding and commitment to our University’s Catholic identity, mission and core values . Applicants invited to interview for faculty and select leadership positions will meet with a senior member of the university to discuss Ex Corde Ecclesiae as a part of the hiring process. Current Job Openings Keywords Location Remote positions only Category Part Time Staff Adjunct Faculty Full Time On Call Your browser does not support JavaScript, or it is disabled. JavaScript must be enabled in order to view listings. Load more listings Equal Employment Opportunity Statement In order to provide equal employment and advancement opportunities to all individuals, employment decisions at University of Saint Francis will be based on merit, qualifications, and abilities. The University does not discriminate in employment opportunities or practices on the basis of age, race, religion, national origin, sex, disability, genetics, and veteran status. The University of Saint Francis (SF) is a Catholic, Franciscan institution and reserves the right to make employment and education decisions based upon religion. Title IX The University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory learning, living, and working environment for all members of the University community. In accordance with the provisions of Title IX of the Higher Education Amendments Act (Title IX), the University does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in any of its education or employment programs and activities.  For more information, to access the Title IX policy or to report a potential violation of Title IX, please contact the University’s Title IX Coordinator, Jay Segal at jsegal@sf.edu or at 260-399-7700, ext. 6741. The University also does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of any other protected characteristic (such as race, national origin, age, disability, etc.), and any such concerns or complaints may be reported to hr@sf.edu . To request an accommodation based upon a protected characteristic, such as disability, please contact hr@sf.edu . Employment Law Applicants to and employees of most private employers, state and local governments, educational institutions, employment agencies and labor organizations are protected under Federal law from discrimination. Contact Us Human Resources St. Michael Hall Offices 203-205 Email: hr@sf.edu Hours Monday – Friday: 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    },
    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/professional-development/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Professional Development - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Professional Development In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here Professional Development In keeping with its commitment to lifelong learning, the University of Saint Francis provides employees with ample professional development opportunities. Additionally, employees are encouraged to participate in leadership and service programs — a reflection of the community’s mission and core values . Professional development opportunities include, but are not limited to, the following: Learn Employee Development Day Fort Wayne Teaching and Learning Conference Faculty Development Funds Tuition Benefit Program Lead Faculty Peer Mentoring Association of Franciscan Colleges and Universities Symposium Franciscan Formation for Employees Program Leadership roles in shared governance Serve Mission Leave U Can Crush Hunger Food Drive Formula for Life Welcome Weekend and New Student Move-In Contact Us Human Resources St. Michael Hall Offices 203-205 Email: hr@sf.edu Hours Monday – Friday: 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    },
    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/working-here/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Working Here - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Careers Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here The Saint Francis Community The University of Saint Francis provides an exemplary academic experience for students and joyful service for our community’s constituents. The outcome of our collective behaviors has become “The Saint Francis Way.” Further, articulating our cultural behaviors in relation to our core values strengthens our ability to educate and serve while helping the university differentiate itself as a quality organization. To that end, we have created mission-driven standards for service quality at Saint Francis. When we take personal responsibility by embracing these behaviors, we advance the hallmark of quality for which our university is known. Employees provide the intellect, empathy, and ability to serve our students and community. The Saint Francis Way of serving has become a source of pride for many employees. To provide a consistently high level of quality experience across our university, we provide the following service expectations for all employees. These standards have been incorporated into ongoing employee performance evaluations. Provide opportunities for deeper conversations and spiritual reflection or prayer in class, at Saint Francis events, and online. Utilize best practices in communication and service. Add best practices suited to your position and responsibilities. Apply care to your words and deeds to ensure respect for others, especially when dealing with delicate matters. Commit to details by following through and/or following up without exception and with quality. Offer additional assistance after serving someone or solving a problem, as in, “How else may I assist you?” Respond promptly, whether in person, via phone, or email. Recognize and celebrate milestones and achievements. Use resources wisely and support green initiatives. Mass and Adoration Time Offices remain open during Mass time, but campus-sponsored activities are not scheduled during that time. This allows students or employees on main campus to attend Mass if they wish to do so. When Mass is offered on campus or at a university location, employees at that location may do so as part of their normal work hours. When Eucharistic Adoration is available on campus or at a university location and during normal work hours, employees who wish to participate may also use a half hour per week for Eucharistic Adoration as part of their normal work hours. Employee Events We offer various employee events throughout the year that foster fellowship and promote employee development. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    },
    "https://www.sf.edu/about/offices-and-departments/careers/": {
      "title": "Find a Program",
      "description": "Careers - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 72 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Careers In this section Offices and Departments Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here In this section Offices and Departments Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here Working at Saint Francis The University of Saint Francis is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified faculty and staff. As such, our Human Resources department works to match each employee to a position that: Maximizes his/her professional expertise, qualifications, and potential Inspires personal and professional growth Cultivates collaboration and teamwork Focuses on the academic, spiritual, and personal growth of our students The University of Saint Francis was founded by the Sisters of St. Francis of Perpetual Adoration in 1890. Throughout its existence, Saint Francis has held firm to its founding ideals as a Catholic university. All decisions related to the university’s growth and future development are evaluated through the lens of its mission and core values. Learn more about our community and “The Saint Francis Way!” See our current job openings and learn about our careers. Information in this section Awards and Recognition Benefits Current Openings Professional Development Working Here You’ll Love Fort Wayne Fort Wayne is a diverse, vibrant, and family-oriented community. As the state’s second-largest city, it is home to an array of businesses, art, culture, athletics, and more. The Fort Wayne area offers great school systems and a low cost of living. Greater Fort Wayne Visit Fort Wayne 2025 1095-C Tax Information 1095 Tax Form Notice Manual 1095 Request Form WEX ACA Participation Portal Guide Contact Us Human Resources St. Michael Hall Offices 203-205 Email: hr@sf.edu Hours Monday – Friday: 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News © 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"
    }
  },
